join char_owen center
char_chef_bot_narration: Owen walks in carrying a spatula. He looks at one of my arms, a bent and cracking version of the tool in his hand hanging limp at my side.
char_owen: Hey, Chops! Can you take a break for a minute? I've got that replacement arm for you.
cha_chef_bot: One second!
char_chef_bot_narration: I take the slightly-burnt food off the stove and send the Bowl-Bots to their charging stations.
cha_chef_bot: Thank you, Owen.
char_owen: My pleasure.
char_chef_bot_narration: He gets to work fixing my arm.
char_owen: Be careful, okay? The financials aren't looking good.
char_owen: I won't be able to order any more replacement parts for a while. We'll have to make do with what I've got in storage.
cha_chef_bot: Don't worry, Owen. I will be.
char_owen: I'm tired of putting up with the Company's bullshit! Don't they see how important the work we're doing here is?
char_owen: Ever since that asshole Sampson Grey was made CEO, he's been putting all the funds towards his pet project of extending human lifetime and cutting everything that actually matters!
cha_chef_bot: I'm sorry, Owen. That sounds tough.
char_owen: There. All done!
char_chef_bot_narration: He steps back and I lift up my newly repaired arm. I test it by picking up a slice of Buglemelon and placing it on the grill.
cha_chef_bot: Thank you, Owen.
char_owen: No problem! Let me know if anything starts to fail. The earlier I can repair something, the easier it will be.
cha_chef_bot: Will do, Owen.